></p><p> </p><p style=3D"text-align:left;"><span>The <a href=3D"https://www=
.metatrader5.com/en/terminal/help/indicators/bw_indicators/fractals" target=
=3D"_blank" title=3D"MetaTrader 5 Help: Fractals Indicator" class=3D"linkat=
or"><span class=3D"mark">Fractal</span></a> Dimension Index determines the =
amount of market volatility.</span></p> <p style=3D"text-align:left;"><span=
>The easiest way to use this indicator is to understand that a value of 1.5=
 suggests the market is acting in a completely random fashion.</span><span>=
</span><span></span><span><span></span><span></span>.<span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp; </span></span><span></span></p> <p style=3D"text-align:left;"><span>A=
s the market deviates from 1.5, the opportunity for earning profits is incr=
eased in proportion to the amount of deviation.</span><span></span><span></=
span><span><span></span><span></span><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span=
></span></p> <p style=3D"text-align:left;"><span>But be careful, the indica=
tor does not show the direction of trend.</span><span></span><span></span><=
span><span></span><span></span><span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span></span></p> <p style=
=3D"text-align:left;"><span>The indicator is RED when the market is in a tr=
end. And it is blue when there is a high volatility</span><span></span><spa=
n></span><span><span></span><span></span>.<span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nb=
sp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span></span></p> <p style=3D"tex=
t-align:left;"><span>When the FDI changes its color from red to blue, it me=
ans that a trend is finishing, the market becomes</span><span></span><span>=
</span><span><span></span><span></span> </span><span>erratic and a high vol=
atility is present. Usually, these "blue times" do not go for a long time. =
They come before a new trend.</span><span></span><span></span><span><span><=
